  "shortName": "NE 115",
  "region": "Northeast US (New England, Adirondacks, Catskills)",
  "country": "US",
  "description": "The Northeast 111 plus four: the 67 New England 4,000-footers, the 46 Adirondack High Peaks and Slide and Hunter in the Catskills. Commonly still called the Northeast 111.",
  "criteria": "All 67 AMC New England 4,000-footers (48 NH, 14 ME, 5 VT), all 46 Adirondack High Peaks (traditional list, including four below 4,000 ft by modern surveys), and Slide and Hunter Mountains in the Catskills. 67 + 46 + 2 = 115.",
  "organization": "Northeast 111ers (community list; NE New England AMC / Adirondack 46er / Catskill 3500 definitions for component lists)",
  "officialUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northeast_111",
  "notes": "Per Wikipedia, the list has 115 peaks but is still called the Northeast 111 because the name predates later additions. The four extra peaks are Adirondack peaks under 4,000 ft by modern surveys: Blake Peak, Cliff Mountain, Nye Mountain and Couchsachraga Peak (marked in notes). Removing them gives the 'true' 111, an inference from Wikipedia's wording; confirm against the NE111 organization if it matters. New England elevations follow the AMC Four Thousand Footer Committee table (e.g. Lafayette 5260, Tecumseh 4003; some Wikipedia tables show 5249 and 3997). Adirondack elevations are the traditional 46er values. Slide (4185) and Hunter (4030) use Catskill 3500 Club figures so shared peak slugs match catskill-3500.json. Some New England ranges are approximate groupings. Winter and sub-peak rules: Katahdin's Baxter and Hamlin, Bigelow West and Avery, both Kinsmans, both Hancocks, Tripyramid North and Middle, and Wildcat A and D are separate peaks. No coordinates included for New England peaks.",
